Patch 2041: the common vertex formats decoded with fixed component counts and tables (VF_UNROLL=0 off).

In the demo fights read_vp_vertex_fast was 26% of the drawing thread (sampled profile). Per array attribute and vertex it ran
a switch on the type and a loop over the component count. Now float32 x1-x4, half x2-x4 and u8-normalized x3-x4 are decoded
with the count fixed per case, float words byte-swapped as words, half floats and u8 normalized through tables (64K and 256
entries, filled from rsx_rd_half_be and the same multiply, so the values are the same: half denormals still read as zero).
Other formats take the loops as before.

Tested (US disc, attract demo, demo fights 180-520 s, three on/off pairs, same build): on 18.46 / 17.28 / 18.53 flips/s,
off 17.55 / 16.20 / 17.37; on was faster in every pair, by about 1 flip/s.

